  "name": "β 2 MICROGLOBULIN URINE SPOT",
  "code": "1342",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>-Beta-2-microglobulin (beta-2-MG) is a small membrane protein associated with the heavy chains of class I HLA proteins and hence is<br>present on the surface of all nucleated cells.<br>-Urine beta-2-microglobulin levels are elevated in diseases associated with increased cell turnover with several benign conditions such as<br>chronic systemic inflammation, liver disease, renal dysfunction, some acute viral infection.<br>-Malignancies, especially hematologic malignancies associated with the B-lymphocyte lineage &amp; plasma cell disorders, in multiple myeloma;<br>beta-2-microglobulin is considered as a powerful prognostic factor.</p>",
